plies:\n\\[ xy + yz + zx = 2xyz \\]\n\nWe need to find the value of:\n\\[ \\frac{x + y}{z} + \\frac{y + z}{x} + \\frac{x + z}{y} \\]\n\nWe can rewrite this expression as:\n\\[ \\frac{x + y}{z} + \\frac{y + z}{x} + \\frac{x + z}{y} = \\frac{x}{z} + \\frac{y}{z} + \\frac{y}{x} + \\frac{z}{x} + \\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{z}{y} \\]\n\nThis can be further simplified to:\n\\[ \\frac{x}{z} + \\frac{y}{z} + \\frac{y}{x} + \\frac{z}{x} + \\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{z}{y} = \\frac{x + y + z}{z} + \\frac{x + y + z}{x} + \\frac{x + y + z}{y} - 3 \\]\n\nUsing the fact that \\( x + y + z = 6 \\), we get:\n\\[ \\frac{x + y + z}{z} + \\frac{x + y + z}{x} + \\frac{x + y + z}{y} - 3 = \\frac{6}{z} + \\frac{6}{x} + \\frac{6}{y} - 3 = 6 \\left( \\frac{1}{z} + \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} \\right) - 3 \\]\n\nSince we know that:\n\\[ \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z} = 2 \\]\n\nWe substitute this value in:\n\\[ 6 \\left( \\frac{1}{z} + \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} \\right) - 3 = 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 = 12 - 3 = 9 \\]\n\nThus, the value is:\n\\[ \\boxed{9} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{9}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:309"}
